<title>SPAIN: Lira in ERM further step toward EMU - Spain Folgado.</title>
<headline>Lira in ERM further step toward EMU - Spain Folgado.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1996-11-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Italian lira's re-entry into the ERM strengthened the committment of almost all the European Union's countries to enter European Monetary Union (EMU) from the start, Spain's Budget Secretary Jose Folgado said on Monday.</p>
<p>&quot;(The lira re-entry) is a positive factor, which shows the political willingnes of almost every national government to join (the European monetary Union) from its start,&quot; Folgado told reporters earlier this morning.</p>
<p>Folgado added that, for the first time in a long time, economic prospects in Europe were very good after national states corrected structural imbalances in public deficit, inflation and balance of payments.</p>
<p>&quot;There have been eliminating bottlenecks in the economy of their countries,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>-- Madrid Newsroom, +341 585 8340</p>
</text>
